body:
The `if` statement is missing braces, so only `console.log(...)` is conditional and `pm.environment.set(...)` will run even when `user_id` is `undefined`. Wrap the logging + environment assignment in braces (and consider guarding `responseJson.items?.[0]?.id` to avoid script errors when the list is empty).
```suggestion
      const user_id = responseJson.items?.[0]?.id;

      if (user_id != undefined) {
          console.log("Setting user id:", user_id);
          pm.environment.set("user_id", user_id);
      }
```
